('irk','Hajj is performed in the month of','["Ramadan","Rajab","Dhul-Hijjah","Safar"]'::jsonb,2,'It is the twelfth month of the Islamic calendar.'),
('irk','Eid al-Fitr marks the end of','["Hajj","Ramadan","Muharram","Rajab"]'::jsonb,1,'Muslims celebrate with prayer and charity.'),
('irk','Eid al-Adha remembers the willingness of Prophet Ibrahim (AS) to','["sacrifice his son for Allah","leave his homeland","destroy idols","build the Ka''bah alone"]'::jsonb,0,'Allah replaced the son with a ram.'),
('irk','The first revelation of the Qur''an came to the Prophet (SAW) in the cave of','["Thawr","Uhud","Safa","Hira"]'::jsonb,3,'It was on Mount Nur near Makkah.'),
('irk','The first word revealed to the Prophet (SAW) was','["Qul (Say)","Salat (Pray)","Iqra (Read)","Amin (Truly)"]'::jsonb,2,'It opens Surah Al-Alaq.'),
('irk','The first Caliph after the Prophet (SAW) was','["Umar","Abu Bakr","Uthman","Ali"]'::jsonb,1,'He was called As-Siddiq.'),
('irk','The number of chapters (surahs) in the Qur''an is','["114","99","120","30"]'::jsonb,0,'The Qur''an is also divided into 30 parts (juz).'),
('irk','The first chapter of the Qur''an is','["Al-Baqarah","Al-Ikhlas","An-Nas","Al-Fatihah"]'::jsonb,3,'It is recited in every rak''ah of prayer.'),
('irk','Muslims face the Ka''bah in Makkah during prayer. This direction is the','["mihrab","minbar","qiblah","adhan"]'::jsonb,2,'It unites Muslims in worship.'),
('irk','The Sunnah is','["the chapters of the Qur''an","the sayings, actions and approvals of the Prophet (SAW)","the Islamic calendar","the pilgrimage rites"]'::jsonb,1,'It is the second source of Islamic law.'),
('irk','Ablution before prayer is called','["wudu","tayammum","ghusl","tawaf"]'::jsonb,0,'It involves washing the face, hands and arms, wiping the head and washing the feet.'),
('irk','When water is not available, a Muslim may perform','["ghusl","sa''i","adhan","tayammum"]'::jsonb,3,'Clean earth or dust is used instead of water.'),
('irk','The special congregational prayer held on Fridays is','["Tarawih","Tahajjud","Jumu''ah","Duha"]'::jsonb,2,'It replaces the Zuhr prayer on that day.'),
('irk','The Shahadah is the','["act of fasting","declaration of faith in Allah and in Muhammad as His messenger","act of giving charity","journey to Makkah"]'::jsonb,1,'Saying it sincerely makes a person a Muslim.'),
('irk','The Prophet''s mother was','["Aminah","Khadijah","Aishah","Fatimah"]'::jsonb,0,'She died when he was a young child.'),
('irk','The first wife of the Prophet (SAW) was','["Aishah","Hafsah","Zaynab","Khadijah"]'::jsonb,3,'She was the first person to accept Islam.'),
('irk','The first major battle between Muslims and the Quraysh was the Battle of','["Uhud","Khandaq","Badr","Hunayn"]'::jsonb,2,'The Muslims won in the second year after the Hijrah.'),
('irk','Zakat al-Fitr is paid','["during Hajj","at the end of Ramadan","in Rajab","at the start of Muharram"]'::jsonb,1,'It purifies the fast and feeds the needy.'),
('irk','Riba, which Islam forbids, means','["interest or usury","charity","trade","inheritance"]'::jsonb,0,'Taking or giving interest on loans is prohibited.'),
('irk','The Qur''an forbids','["trade","marriage","fasting","intoxicants such as alcohol"]'::jsonb,3,'Alcohol is called khamr.'),
('irk','The Ka''bah was rebuilt by Prophet Ibrahim (AS) and his son','["Ishaq (AS)","Yaqub (AS)","Isma''il (AS)","Yusuf (AS)"]'::jsonb,2,'They raised its foundations together.'),
('irk','Walking around the Ka''bah seven times during Hajj or Umrah is','["sa''i","tawaf","ihram","rami"]'::jsonb,1,'It starts at the Black Stone.'),
('irk','Walking between the hills of Safa and Marwa is','["sa''i","tawaf","wuquf","zakat"]'::jsonb,0,'It remembers Hajar''s search for water.'),
('irk','The most important rite of Hajj, performed on the ninth of Dhul-Hijjah, is standing at','["Mina","Muzdalifah","Jamarat","Arafat"]'::jsonb,3,'Hajj is said to be Arafat.'),
('irk','The angel who brought revelation to the prophets was','["Mikail","Israfil","Jibril (Gabriel)","Izra''il"]'::jsonb,2,'He conveyed the Qur''an to the Prophet (SAW).'),
('irk','Muslims believe that the last of the prophets was','["Isa (AS)","Muhammad (SAW)","Musa (AS)","Ibrahim (AS)"]'::jsonb,1,'He is called the Seal of the Prophets.'),
('irk','The four Rightly Guided Caliphs were Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman and','["Ali","Bilal","Khalid","Hamza"]'::jsonb,0,'They led the Muslim community after the Prophet (SAW).'),
('irk','The minimum amount of wealth on which zakat becomes due is the','["sadaqah","fidyah","khums","nisab"]'::jsonb,3,'A person must own at least this amount for a full year.'),
('irk','People who are exempt from fasting in Ramadan include','["students and teachers","traders and farmers","the sick and travellers (who make up the days later)","healthy adults at home"]'::jsonb,2,'The Qur''an allows them to fast later.'),
